From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:25:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sceNpTrophy: a host API (notices, queries, icons), the
 title's language, an atomic store, a lock, a debug block

The port needs to show an unlock as it happens and to list the set, and 5001
gives it nothing but a log line. This adds a host API (sceNpTrophy.h, not
guest functions):

- ps3_trophy_set_notify(fn, user): fn hears every new unlock on the unlocking
  guest thread, then once more for a platinum the unlock completes; never an
  id already unlocked. The notice (comm id, id, grade, hidden, name, detail)
  is valid only during the call, and the store's lock is not held then, so fn
  may query. The notice's layout and the setter follow Project Pyrrhus and
  Project Helghast patch 5004 (MIT), so a port written for one works with
  the other; the code is this project's own.
- ps3_trophy_count, ps3_trophy_get(id): the set and the store (grade, hidden,
  unlocked, time, name and detail in the title's language, the English
  name).
- ps3_trophy_icon(id): TROPnnn.PNG (-1: ICON0.PNG), read from the TRP when
  asked, malloc'd.
- ps3_trophy_set_blocked(1): unlocks are logged "blocked by debug option",
  neither stored nor notified; the title is still told they worked.

Names: TROP_<nn>.SFM for the language PS3_LANG names (a CELL_SYSUTIL_LANG_*
number or its code), when the set has it, else TROP.SFM; the store and the
log keep TROP.SFM's English names. Killzone HD's set has 02 to 06 (fr, es,
de, it, nl).

The JSON store is written to <file>.tmp, flushed (fsync, _commit), then
renamed over the old one (MoveFileExA with MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING on
Windows): a crash mid-save keeps the old file. The format is unchanged. One
mutex guards the contexts: the title's unlock thread writes them while the
port reads them.

Checked with tools/tests/test_trophy_notify.sh (a synthetic TRP): the order
of the notices and the platinum, no repeat, the French names and the
fallback, the store across a reload with no temp file left, the block, the
icon bytes; and in the game (Killzone HD, see the commit).
